    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scum_and_Villainy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy</a></i> </p><p>Droidification is an extensive process that turns a common piece of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a> into a fully functioning <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid\">Droid</a>. The <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a> can either act as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid\">Droid</a> with access to the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a> it was built from, or conceal itself as a normal piece of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a>. While concealing itself as normal <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a>, the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid\">Droid</a> can't take any Actions, and a DC 25 <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Perception\" title=\"Perception\">Perception</a> check is required to realize the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a> is unusual. </p><p>Only devices can receive this Upgrade. Weapons, Armor, and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicles\" title=\"Vehicles\">Vehicles</a> cannot be Droidified. </p><p><i>Example: </i> Deel Surool owns a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Datapad\" title=\"Datapad\">Datapad</a> he'd like to be able to call (like a pet). Since a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Datapad\" title=\"Datapad\">Datapad</a> has only one Upgrade Slot, he increases it's size to Diminutive (due to it's weight, a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Datapad\" title=\"Datapad\">Datapad</a> is a Fine item). He then pays to have it Droidified. This makes it the equivalent of an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/ASP_Labor_Droid\" title=\"ASP Labor Droid\">ASP Labor Droid</a> with <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Strength\" title=\"Strength\">Strength</a> 8, <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Dexterity\" title=\"Dexterity\">Dexterity</a> 15, and a speed of 1 square. Since it is a walking <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Datapad\" title=\"Datapad\">Datapad</a>, Deel programs it to use it's unassigned <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Feat\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Feat\">Feat</a> for <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Skill_Training\" title=\"Skill Training\">Skill Training</a> in <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Use_Computer\" title=\"Use Computer\">Use Computer</a> (giving it <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Use_Computer\" title=\"Use Computer\">Use Computer</a> +3), enough to download data from an unprotected system. </p><p>If any additional <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid_Equipment\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid Equipment\">Droid Equipment</a> or <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid_Systems\" title=\"Droid Systems\">Droid Systems</a> are added to the Droidified <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a>, it becomes obvious that the device is a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid\">Droid</a> rather than the original item. </p>",
